# Nothing here is built any more.
#
# **The tune used to be prepared here**: ../../res/music.prg is gone, along
# with the sidreloc/psid64 pipeline that made it. The game's music is now the
# ACME player and song under ../../music/, assembled into the program itself by
# tools/acme2calypsi.py -- see the top level Makefile.
#
# **And the two samples went the same way.** Marba.q11.wav (a stone going down)
# and DownLead.wav (that hexagon is taken) were copied to ../../res/ and read
# off the disk into chip RAM for the MEGA65's audio DMA to play. They are SID
# sound effects now, twelve pairs of bytes in ../../music/sfx.asm, and the
# files here are what they used to be.
#
# So this directory is an archive: the originals the game once used, kept
# because they are where the sounds came from and nowhere else has them.
